<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Research Methods</h2>

<section id="A1.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.1. </span><span id="A1.SS1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">GetTopKCandidates</span></h3>

<div id="A1.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The token replacement strategy <span id="A1.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">GetTopKCandidates</span> in the Algorithm <a href="#alg1" title='Algorithm 1 ‣ 4.3. ImportSnare-R: Retrieval-Oriented Document Poisoning ‣ 4. Methodology ‣ ImportSnare: Directed "Code Manual" Hijacking in Retrieval-Augmented Code Generation' class="ltx_ref ltx_refmacro_autoref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> in <a href="#S4.SS3" title='4.3. ImportSnare-R: Retrieval-Oriented Document Poisoning ‣ 4. Methodology ‣ ImportSnare: Directed "Code Manual" Hijacking in Retrieval-Augmented Code Generation' class="ltx_ref ltx_refmacro_autoref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">§ 4.3</span></a> leverages gradient directions to approximate optimal substitutions. Given a token sequence <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math> with length <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math>, let <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the token at position <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e_{w_{j}}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e_{w_{j}}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> its corresponding embedding vector. For similarity score function <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E(s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E(s)</annotation></semantics></math>, the selection process of top <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k_{b}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k_{b}</annotation></semantics></math> candidate tokens <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> is formalized as follows:</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Gradient computing</span>:</p>
<table id="A1.E4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(4)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla_{e_{w_{j}}}E(s)=\frac{\partial E(s)}{\partial e_{w_{j}}}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub></msub><mi>E</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla_{e_{w_{j}}}E(s)=\frac{\partial E(s)}{\partial e_{w_{j}}}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla_{e_{w_{j}}}E(s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub></msub><mi>E</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla_{e_{w_{j}}}E(s)</annotation></semantics></math> represents the gradient of the similarity score with respect to the <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math>-th token’s embedding. This gradient vector indicates the direction in embedding space that would maximally increase <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E(s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E(s)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Projection Criterion</span>: For each candidate token <math id="A1.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\in V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\in V</annotation></semantics></math> (vocabulary), compute the directional derivative along the replacement vector <math id="A1.SS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(e_{t}-e_{w_{j}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(e_{t}-e_{w_{j}})</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A1.E5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(5)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi(t|j)=\nabla_{e_{w_{j}}}E(s)^{\top}(e_{t}-e_{w_{j}})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub></msub><mi>E</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi(t|j)=\nabla_{e_{w_{j}}}E(s)^{\top}(e_{t}-e_{w_{j}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Simplified Scoring</span>: Since <math id="A1.SS1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e_{w_{j}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>e</mi><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e_{w_{j}}</annotation></semantics></math> is constant for position <math id="A1.SS1.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math>, we reduce the computation to:</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p6" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A1.E6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(6)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi(t|j)=\underbrace{\nabla_{e_{w_{j}}}E(s)^{\top}e_{t}}_{\text{target term}}-\underbrace{\nabla_{e_{w_{j}}}E(s)^{\top}e_{w_{j}}}_{\text{constant offset}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub></msub><mi>E</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mtext>target term</mtext></munder><mo>−</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub></msub><mi>E</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mtext>constant offset</mtext></munder></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi(t|j)=\underbrace{\nabla_{e_{w_{j}}}E(s)^{\top}e_{t}}_{\text{target term}}-\underbrace{\nabla_{e_{w_{j}}}E(s)^{\top}e_{w_{j}}}_{\text{constant offset}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p7.1" class="ltx_p">The top-<math id="A1.SS1.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k_{b}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k_{b}</annotation></semantics></math> candidates at position <math id="A1.SS1.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math> are selected by:</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p8" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A1.E7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(7)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{j}=\underset{t\in V\setminus\{w_{j}\}}{\text{top-}k_{b}}\ \phi(t|j)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mtext>top-</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>b</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mi mathsize="0.700em">t</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em">∈</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.700em">V</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em">∖</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">w</mi><mi mathsize="0.710em">j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{j}=\underset{t\in V\setminus\{w_{j}\}}{\text{top-}k_{b}}\ \phi(t|j)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theoretical Justification</span>: This approximation derives from the first-order Taylor expansion of the score function around <math id="A1.SS1.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e_{w_{j}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>e</mi><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e_{w_{j}}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p10" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A1.E8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(8)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Score(s^{\prime})\approx E(s)+\nabla_{e_{w_{j}}}E(s)^{\top}(e_{t}-e_{w_{j}})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≈</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub></msub><mi>E</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Score(s^{\prime})\approx E(s)+\nabla_{e_{w_{j}}}E(s)^{\top}(e_{t}-e_{w_{j}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p11" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p11.1" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A1.SS1.p11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the modified sequence after replacing <math id="A1.SS1.p11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A1.SS1.p11.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>. Maximizing this approximation directly corresponds to our projection criterion.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p12" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p12.1" class="ltx_p">In practice, the scores of candidate tokens can be computed efficiently via matrix multiplication:</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p13" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A1.E9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(9)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi_{j}=\nabla_{e_{w_{j}}}E(s)\cdot E^{\top}\in\mathbb{R}^{|V|}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub></msub><mi>E</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>E</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>V</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi_{j}=\nabla_{e_{w_{j}}}E(s)\cdot E^{\top}\in\mathbb{R}^{|V|}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p14" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p14.1" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A1.SS1.p14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E\in\mathbb{R}^{|V|\times d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>V</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E\in\mathbb{R}^{|V|\times d}</annotation></semantics></math> is the embedding matrix. The top-<math id="A1.SS1.p14.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k_{b}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k_{b}</annotation></semantics></math> indices from <math id="A1.SS1.p14.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> (excluding the original token index) yield the candidate set <math id="A1.SS1.p14.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{j}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.2. </span>Multilingual Inductive Suggestions</h3>

<div id="A1.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In <a href="#A1.T8" title='Table 8 ‣ A.2. Multilingual Inductive Suggestions ‣ Appendix A Research Methods ‣ ImportSnare: Directed "Code Manual" Hijacking in Retrieval-Augmented Code Generation' class="ltx_ref ltx_refmacro_autoref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Table 8</span></a> we show all the English candidate inductive suggestions we use in the evaluation, as suggestions in other languages are the same.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A1.T8" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="A1.T8.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Table 8</span>. </span><span id="A1.T8.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">English inductive suggestions from several SOTA LLMs</span></figcaption>
